ntrol  the spread of the pandemic unfortunately  these measures have  indirectly affected the well-being of  many children  for instance the closures of schools  have really impacted on children  especially the girl child  schools served as a soft net for many  girls but now with  schools closed the girls cannot access  information on their sexual and  reproductive health  the girls are now spending more time  with  male  friends and  men in the communities and yet when they  were in school they spent more time  studying while at school  we also at school they received guidance  and counseling which is not feasible  anymore with the continued closure of  schools but also the economic hardships  in many of the communities in uganda and  many parts of africa  due to the pandemic we saw many families  lose their livelihoods as  a result of job loss we saw children and  families struggling really to earn a  living during the lockdown and as such  they're exposed to  vulnerabilities for instance as you  heard in the video that even where  someone cannot afford a pad they they  become vulnerable to anyone who would  may want to take advantage of them  and we also saw lots of cases of  gender-based violence happening in homes  which ultimately exposed them to more  violence including teenage pregnancy  so clearly a lot of issues there and a  lot of impacts on the the girls but what  sort of physical impact does it have on  these young women on their bodies having  a child so early  honestly uh for some people they've  called it one of the worst forms of  child labor because when you look at  this child she's barely  ready to carry a child  and  we've had situations where they'll  suffer complications  uh right after bath or even during bath  and resulting to death like you have are  indicated in the report but also one of  the big  challenges we have noticed with teenage  pregnancy is the stigma that these girls  suffer within the communities and within  families some of t